            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0746" n="632" xml:id="pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">551.5F1/189: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-19T16:00:00-05:00">November 19, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>331. If participation of the great powers, especially the United States and Great
                    Britain, is assured, Mexico will probably issue a call to an international
                    conference on silver: the place, Mexico City; the time, this winter. This
                    Government distinctly favors the conference idea, and hopes that the British
                    will see fit to accept the invitation. Please sound them out on this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
